          "comment": "[Playbook] We revised the assignment clause so we may assign freely to an affiliate or to a successor in a merger, acquisition or sale of substantially all assets, without the competitor carve-back that would let Commerce One block our corporate transactions, and so Commerce One may assign only with our consent (not unreasonably withheld) and never to our competitor. This reflects our standard position that a vendor should not gain leverage over our M&A activity; if helpful, we can accept a mutual notice-based successor right with consent not unreasonably withheld for other assignments.",
